WEBVTT

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.750
The year sure went by fast.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:38.310
Huh?

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.750
I was thinking, "Ah, it's the season when the freshmen arrive."

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.260
Ah, yeah it is.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.460
It's already been a year.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.340
I wonder if there will be new members joining us this year.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.150
Hey, didn't Kasukabe-san chase all of them away last year?

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.210
Ah, she did.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:59.830
<i>How do I say this... I don't feel like telling my name to otakus?</i>

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:04.770
<i>Let me say this first: even though it's freshman season, I have no intention of accepting them.</i>

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:12.160
Well, it seems that Kasukabe-san is starting to act a little coy.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.270
Eh, really?

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.070
What, you don't think so?

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:20.470
Move it towards the top-right a bit more.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:21.870
Okay.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.330
How do you feel about the second season of Kujian?

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.260
Well, I didn't expect them to make one, so I feel that it's just "all right" because of that.

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.000
I guess.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:39.940
I hope they manage to maintain some sort of quality and not drag it out.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.170
Anime can turn people into adults, can't it?

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.260
What kind of adult?

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.100
This is Kugayama-san's, isn't it?

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.710
Yeah, I think so. It's probably his.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:53.920
I think it's best that we return it to him, but he hasn't been to the clubroom lately.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.360
I guess he's been busy job-hunting. It seems that his parents have some expectations of him.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.010
Oh...

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.830
Tanaka-san and Ohno-san seem to have gone to Nippori...

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:06.910
They're really easy-going.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.530
The two of them get along really well.

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.270
They are fellow cosplayers after all.

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.490
Is your job hunt going well?

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.240
U-Uh, me?

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:20.670
Hey, who is that?

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.120
Hello.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.640
H-Hello.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.210
You're Kuchiki-kun, right?

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.600
I thought you joined the Anime Society?
What's wrong?

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:38.430
Actually, I've come here in pursuit of knowledge.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:40.570
Eh? Pursuit of knowledge? What kind?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.850
Fighting games.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.200
Select your team members!

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.940
Hey, can you do it?

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.600
Well, I'm just buying time until Kohsaka-kun arrives.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.750
Once he arrives, he'll crush him completely.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.480
How evil.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.430
You seem to have grown stronger.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.270
So what did you mean by "pursuit of knowledge"?

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:18.230
That was a lie.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:19.700
Huh?

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.170
Huh? Aren't you Kucchi? Why are you here?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.310
Yes, yes! No one calls me "Kucchi" in the Anime Society!

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.080
Ah, I'm so touched!

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.960
No one understands me!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.220
By the way, what's up with him?

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.160
Well, we're not sure of what's going on either.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:50.050
Well, to summarize, I'm going to keep my explanation plain,
simple, straightforward, and easy to understand.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.000
The only person who calls me by the name "Kucchi" is calling out to me!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.070
She is none other than Madam Kasukabe who leads the Society for the Study of Modern Visual Culture.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.860
I am willing to devote my all to the creation of this new generation!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.380
Isn't that straightforwardness great?

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.580
It makes me happy!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.700
Well, does that mean you wish to join us?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.250
It's like you...

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.120
Hey, what's wrong?

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.380
You were going berserk, weren't you? I'll kick you out if you hit me.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:35.350
I'm sorry. Please let me join the Genshiken.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.500
Why didn't you say that from the start?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.420
Okay.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:39.150
Eh?!

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:45.270
I did it! Yahoo!

00:05:45.270 --> 00:05:46.110
Is it okay?

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.070
Huh? About?

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.000
Oh...

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.520
She has indeed become coy.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.500
Isn't it more like she doesn't give a damn?

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:58.960
Shut up!

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:09.020
Now, come at me!

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:10.030
I'm going!

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.350
The weather sure is nice.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:18.790
A-As I thought, you like spring, don't you?

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:22.490
Huh? I do like it, but...
Why did you say "as I thought?"

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.530
Do you think such tricks are effective against me?!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:30.690
W-What?!

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.500
What?

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.440
What happened?

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:41.040
Well, it sounds like a fight, but I don't see anything.
It's taking place on the second floor of the opposite building.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.420
Where?

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.520
Ah, there?

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.960
Isn't that the Manga Society?

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:47.710
Ah!

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:49.160
W-What is that?!

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.000
Ah, someone fell!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.090
Huh? Seriously?

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.490
Or should I say that someone jumped?

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.630
W-What's going on?

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.230
Are they all right?

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:05.550
Should we call an ambulance?

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.860
Er... well...

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.680
I think their members will do something...

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:15.610
Well...

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.800
I guess you have all heard the rumors.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.580
Our girls were having some trouble with the new female freshman.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:29.530
S-So, it's embarrassing, but I have a favor to ask of you...

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:33.110
Can the Genshiken take the girl in?

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:37.260
What should we do?

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.370
Regarding those "troubles", which side started it?

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:45.690
There's a 90% chance that it's the girl.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.980
You intend to dump such a person onto us?

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:52.510
Well, she did say that she wanted to at least join a circle dabbling in this area...

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.240
If it's the Genshiken, the number of members is low, everyone gets along with each other...

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:58.360
Well, we have tons of our own problems.

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.200
Is that so?

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.250
Even so, won't we be attracting the grudge of the girls from the Manga Society?

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.530
A-Ah... that probably won't be a problem.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.930
Why? A woman's grudge is pretty scary.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.240
To tell the truth...

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:18.390
All the female members of the Genshiken are already hated by the girls.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:22.230
Even if we add one more now, there won't be much of a difference.

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.910
How can that be?! I understand if it's Saki-san...

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.280
You actually said that...

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:29.610
Well, let's take a look at her first?

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.760
Since Takanayagi-kun seems to be suffering.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:36.530
Ah... you have helped me a lot by saying that!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.800
It's troublesome to be caught between women, isn't it?

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:39.970
That's true!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:45.920
Well... since Kasukabe-san said it...

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.980
Ah, then, President-kun...

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.250
Eh? Now?

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:56.790
Bandaged girl?

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:58.220
An unsociable character?

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:59.930
Is she just faking it?

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.480
No matter how you look at her, she looks petite.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.060
Then, how about a self-introduction?

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:06.690
Yes.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.400
I am the otaku-hating Ogiue.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.830
I especially hate female otakus.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:19.290
Well, she's that kind of person...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.270
Why do you like those homos so much?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.950
Hey, hey. I don't know what happened at the Manga Society, but...

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:28.690
you shouldn't say that all of a sudden, right?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.210
Aren't you an otaku too?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:31.420
You're one too.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.860
Kasukabe-san! Calm down!
You must calm down!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:41.600
Yes, that's right!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.690
I've become coy too!

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.850
It's because my boyfriend is here!

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.000
E-Eh?

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:51.110
Just being here doesn't make me an otaku at all!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:51.940
Understand?

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:54.400
You aren't an otaku?

00:09:54.930 --> 00:09:57.740
Hey, Ohno! You should say something too!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.740
Eh? O-Okay.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.040
There aren't any girls who hate homos!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.160
Does that include me as well?

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:11.520
Of course!

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:22.580
So she jumped from the Manga Society after something like this happened. Right, Takanayagi-kun?

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.260
Ah... that's right.

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.710
I wonder why you jumped off. Doesn't that mean you lost?

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.460
They were insulting me.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:34.750
Ouch ouch ouch...

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:40.220
Before you talk about homos or other such hobbies,
the way you give people headaches is pretty otaku-like.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.650
Wanting to join a circle... Doesn't that mean you're looking for friends?

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:47.300
You should do something about that first.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:49.000
Well, well!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:53.440
Be it Senpai or the newcomer, we should get along
with each other Japanese style, well well!

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:58.390
Let's treat it like nothing has happened here.
Let's say nothing out loud.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:59.720
Nothing.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.090
That sounds so lame!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.220
This person is strange.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:06.640
Wow, again!

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:12.550
He stopped.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.430
Or did he stop because he was stared at?

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.160
Eh? You sure have guts...

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:16.900
Ah!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:19.860
What are you doing?!

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:27.520
Stay there and burn!
You actually assaulted a woman!

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:30.960
Hush, hush, hush.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.570
Eh? Burn?

00:11:32.570 --> 00:11:34.390
How do we do that?

00:11:34.390 --> 00:11:36.040
It seems that he is already burning.

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:04.730
No matter how you look at it, isn't this a bit too obvious?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.910
No. If we don't do that, we won't be able to unveil her true nature.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.250
Oops. She's looking outside.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.020
Look, it does seem a bit weird.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.930
I won't let her discover me.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.190
Erm... well...

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:27.940
Today, Saki-san and Kohsaka-san are out on a date.
Kugayama-san is out searching for a job.

00:12:27.940 --> 00:12:32.160
Kuchiki-kun has gone to Akihabara. The timing is just perfect.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.850
Tanaka, what do you think?

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:39.030
Erm... well... that's...

00:12:39.620 --> 00:12:41.650
Black Ohno has descended, I guess?

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.610
Ah, she's tidying them.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:45.110
That's to be expected.

00:13:12.070 --> 00:13:13.140
Yo...

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.100
Ah?

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.340
Oh? Ogiue, you're alone?

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:18.580
Yes.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:21.050
W-Why is Saki-san...?

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:22.570
Eh? Let me see...

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.770
Ah, indeed...

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:28.570
What happened to their date, their date! Geez, it was the perfect moment...

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:32.540
Kohsaka said that he's going to wander around Akihabara...

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:34.020
So we split up.

00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:36.740
Well, the food was delicious though, so I'll forgive him.

00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.000
It's very troublesome to go out with an otaku.

00:13:40.390 --> 00:13:44.250
Well, it's not really about whether he is an otaku or not.

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.390
Oh? What is this?

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:48.720
Could this be...?

00:13:56.970 --> 00:14:00.290
Ah, I thought so. Ogiue, are these yours?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:05.490
No. They were already here when I came in as if they were for me to read.

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.550
Is that so? Then they must be Ohno's.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.960
Why did she bring so many here?

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.430
I guess she's trying to provoke me.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.130
Ouch ouch.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:18.600
Then, do you want to confirm that?

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:19.800
Huh?

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:23.140
What are they talking about?

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:25.750
Since we can't hear their voices...

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.080
Oh? Saki-san is using her cell phone.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:33.920
Eh? Mine?

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:34.810
Mine?

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.160
Eh, what should I do?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.540
Looks like Saki-san is...

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:41.650
Hello?

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.430
Ah...?

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.710
<i>Ah, it's me, Kasukabe.
Are you free right now?</i>

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:50.150
A-A-Ah... yeah... Free... can be considered to be free now, but...

00:14:50.420 --> 00:14:51.970
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:53.420
<i>Close to the circle?</i>

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:58.120
E-Eh... well if you say circle, I can be
considered to be near a circle I guess...

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.960
<i>Huh? What are you doing?</i>

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:00.500
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:04.520
T-Toilet...

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.550
<i>Ah, there. I'm sorry.</i>

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:08.850
No problem...

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>Then I'll just ask you one thing.</i>

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:12.600
<i>I'm in the clubroom at the moment.</i>

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:15.350
<i>Ohno, is the pile of homo doujinshi yours?</i>

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.770
Yes, they are.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:21.400
<i>Ah, I see. Thanks, that's all. Bye-bye.</i>

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.230
Okay...

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:32.590
It'll be suspicious if I don't
hurry up and head back...

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:34.680
You didn't have to say that much...

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:43.590
What are these...? Look, isn't this from a foreign movie?

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.050
A normal in-house one.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:46.990
I've seen it before.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:52.270
But the people who drew these... Were they thinking about all these when they watched it?

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.390
It's rather amazing.

00:15:54.870 --> 00:15:56.840
I've never thought about that before.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:01.040
That's why the brain structures of those people are weird.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:06.020
Ah, by the way, the male otakus go buy ero doujinshi.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.750
Is it to satisfy their needs?

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:16.480
Do female otaku read such things and [CENSORED]?

00:16:16.480 --> 00:16:17.920
I don't know!

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:23.120
Well, I don't feel anything at all reading such things.

00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:28.030
But Ogiue, since you said you hate these things,
does that mean you've read them before?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:30.410
Or else you wouldn't be complaining about them, right?

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.600
Is this a lead-in question?

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:35.090
But that's true, isn't it?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:41.270
I first read it when I was a fifth-grader. It was from a friend.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.250
<i>Wow, society is hopeless.</i>

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:46.500
You were traumatized from that?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.080
Well... you can say that.

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.220
Ah, that's bad. That's really nasty.

00:16:57.460 --> 00:17:00.360
Hey, what are they talking about?

00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.160
Well...

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:03.720
Can't you plant a bug?!

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:05.140
I couldn't.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.310
It can't be helped, then. I'm going.

00:17:11.310 --> 00:17:12.460
Oh? Is that so?

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.790
Well, our surprise attempt has failed, right?

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.380
It's meaningless to keep looking.

00:17:17.290 --> 00:17:19.280
Remember to go back at a suitable time.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:20.540
Okay...

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:24.590
Hey, will Ohno-san be okay?

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:30.180
Well... if you ask me whether she's going to be okay or not.... Probably not...

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.190
It sure is troublesome.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.320
What do you like if you hate homos? Anime?

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:37.640
Yes... Well...

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:39.660
I do play games.

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:44.860
But in reality, female gamers aren't that rare, right?

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:47.840
Males play games even if they aren't otakus,

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:51.660
but among the friends I know, there aren't many who play games.

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.840
How would I know that?

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.050
Hello.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:58.770
Ah, Ohno. Hello.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:01.720
You sure took your time.
Having bad constipation?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:05.930
P-Please don't say things like that just because there are only females here.

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:09.900
Eh? I was much more direct when I was in girls' high school.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:26.000
U-Um... I asked Ogiue earlier why she hates homos,
and it seems that she has some sort of trauma.

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:28.950
Please don't say it out loud.
I don't want others to know.

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.920
Please don't say it out loud.
I don't want to know.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.050
Ah...

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:39.640
Looks like the atmosphere turned bad quickly...

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.330
Should we start to go back one after another?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:44.870
We have to make it look natural, right?

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:48.290
My, you started to read yaoi books when you were a fifth-grader?

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:52.860
You were traumatized just from that? Unbelievable.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:57.520
In America, girls at that age are already [CENSORED].

00:18:57.520 --> 00:19:02.320
Don't say things like that just because there are only females here, and don't say it facing me.

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:06.780
Isn't it natural for people to get more into it because of stuff like that?

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:11.260
You should be ashamed, forcing your own values onto others.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:16.750
My, looks like I was right. She's trying hard to change the topic.

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:21.760
After all, isn't she an otaku too?

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.490
How could she suffer trauma, right?

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.410
As I was saying, don't say that to me.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.870
Isn't someone who's trying hard to conceal lies even more shameful?

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:36.100
Hey Saki-san, these kind of people will easily...

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:41.060
You [CENSORED] while reading this, don't you?!

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.530
Hey, don't say things like that just because there are only females here...

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:47.870
THIS is what I [CENSORED] to!

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:53.350
<i>Someone... someone please
come and save me...!</i>

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:57.170
Hello!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.760
Oh? Has the meeting already ended?

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:06.670
Oh, Ogi-chin, how nice!
It's great that you're here!

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.290
Ogi-chin?

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:11.130
Ogi-chin, Sunday, yesterday, you went to the Tosanbou.

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:11.760
Eh?!

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.960
Ah, I was there by chance for another event.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:15.430
Huh?

00:20:15.430 --> 00:20:15.960
Hmm?

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:21.170
I actually spotted Ogi-chin at the Scram Dunk:
Mitsugure X Koi Event.

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:23.130
Look, I took a video too.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:26.120
What is that? An otaku-related event?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.080
Of course. It was a yaoi-related event.

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:30.940
Sneaking camera shots?

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.330
I guess so.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.940
Are you an idiot?!

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:45.020
Even though life has become more convenient, people are getting more useless!

00:20:45.020 --> 00:20:46.430
You are an example of that!

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:49.390
Ah, calm down, Ogi-chin.

00:20:49.560 --> 00:20:53.480
E-Erm... M-My brother wanted it.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.080
Oh, brother! You have one?

00:20:56.080 --> 00:20:59.050
B-B-Brother... B-Brother wanted...

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:02.390
Hep wasked mie...

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.180
My brother plays basketball!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:07.920
Oh! I see!

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:15.890
This is the third floor!

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.860
Hey Ohno, come and help!

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:20.060
Ah, oh no!

00:21:20.410 --> 00:21:22.780
W-What happened?

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:26.730
Don't ask "What happened?" Hurry and hold her down!

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:40.010
Wh-What happened?

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:24.930
Eh, the guest we have this time is our new member, Ogiue Chika-san.

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:26.460
Applause.

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:29.010
W-What is this for?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:33.830
When we talk about Ogiue-san, we are reminded of the intimidating moment when she said, "I am the otaku-hating Ogiue."

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:34.830
I don't remember that.

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:38.270
Can we expect more epic lines from you?

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:39.410
What epic lines...?

00:23:39.410 --> 00:23:42.000
Eh? Epic lines are essential for character building!

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.080
It isn't too far out to say that they can determine everything!

00:23:45.080 --> 00:23:48.510
I hope you bring a unique style to our Genshiken.

00:23:48.510 --> 00:23:49.400
I won't bring anything!
